         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Introduction\n\nIn the previous class, we learned that multiplication is adding the same number many times. Independent of the objects we are adding, the result never changes.\n\nAs a consequence, we can organize all these results in a table and use it whenever we need them. We call this table a **multiplication table**.\n\nIn this class, we will learn what a multiplication table is and how we are going to mount it.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
