         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Thinking\n\nPeople normally have 5 fingers on each hand. Now think about the **hands of 10 people** — that is, 10 groups of 5 fingers.\n\nIf I start counting by 5 — 5, 10, 15, 20, and so on — will I always obtain the same results, independent of the people whose fingers I count?",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "8de63808-3672-4216-875d-adbe6767f6f1",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": "yes",
         "score": 2,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "8de63808-3672-4216-875d-adbe6767f6f1",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "4a65633e-9907-4ee1-92b1-091f879064d8",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=4a65633e-9907-4ee1-92b1-091f879064d8",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "fc77d792-25d3-4c13-ace0-0378f3aaec70",
               "text": "Weisstein, Eric W.",
               "page": "https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Multiplication.html",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2024",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Step by Step\n\nIndependent of the selected people, counting their fingers by 5 will always give the same results. And what is true for 5 is true for every other number: when we repeat an addition, the results never change.\n\nBecause of this, we do not need to recalculate them every time. We can organize the results in a table, ready for whenever we need them. To do this, we are going to follow the steps below:\n\n- We will define a **maximum** of repeated values for our table.\n- We will understand the **consequences** of this definition.\n- We will study some **examples** in the next classes.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "585199ad-17d5-4a97-be94-291fb5b2c340",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "585199ad-17d5-4a97-be94-291fb5b2c340",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "nerd",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "4a65633e-9907-4ee1-92b1-091f879064d8",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=4a65633e-9907-4ee1-92b1-091f879064d8",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Step 1: Ten Repeats\n\nRemember: in each order — each family of numbers — we can only write values from **0 to 9**. There is no other single value inside one order.\n\nFor this reason, we will define our tables as having **10 different values**. This means that, for each number we begin to count repeatedly, we are going to repeat it **10 times**: once for each value from 0 to 9.\n\nFor example, the table of 5 contains ten results:\n\n- 5 × 0 = 0\n- 5 × 1 = 5\n- 5 × 2 = 10\n- ...\n- 5 × 9 = 45\n\nOnce the tenth repeat is done, our table is complete.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "ab406443-d516-454d-b700-1870715cdd4a",
         "prev": "",
